apple's iphone event just finished and  they finally revealed  their brand new iphone 12 lineup so in  this video i'm gonna go through all of  the new features and benefits  of the pro models specifically  compared to the previous iphone 11 pro  models  to help you decide if you should  actually make the upgrade  first off as you guys probably already  know the iphone 12 pro max model isn't  going to be shipping until  next month while the regular 6.1 inch  pro model  will start shipping next week and what's  interesting is that this year  the larger max model is getting some  exclusive features  that you can't get on the regular model  and we'll get into those in just a  minute but first let's go over all of  the new features and specs  of apple's brand new iphone 12 pro  the biggest change is the new flat edge  design with surgical grade stainless  steel  which looks really nice and premium and  we also get a brand new color  pacific blue the regular pro model  retains the 6.1 inch display  while the pro max goes up to 6.7 inches  and both of them got a bit more tall  compared to the  11 pro models and they actually got  quite a bit thinner  7.4 millimeters compared to 8.1  on the iphone 11 pro models the 12 pro  models are also just slightly heavier  than the 11 pros 1 gram for the regular  pro model  and 2 grams heavier for the pro max and  while the notch stayed  the exact same size it actually looks a  bit  smaller due to the display bezels  becoming a bit  thinner as well as far as the display  quality it's basically staying  exactly the same compared to the iphone  11 pro  so you get the same 1200 nits of peak  brightness around the same 458 to 460  pixels per inch and everything else  the main difference is the new ceramic  shield glass front  which apple says is four times more  resistant to drops  than the iphone 11 lineup as far as  water resistance  the iphone 12 models now get ip68  rated at up to 6 meters for 30 minutes  compared to 4 meters on the 11 pro  models  the iphone 12 lineup of course gets the  brand new a14 bionic chip  built on the all-new 5 nanometer  architecture  with improvements in everything from the  processor and the gpu  to the neural engine and the machine  learning accelerators  of course a huge feature is the new 5g  modems  supporting both sub 6 and millimeter  wave  in cities that support it so it enables  features like 1080p  facetime video calling over 5g instead  of  only on wi-fi like before apple also  added the new smart data mode  which automatically switches to lte to  save battery life  when you don't need 5g speeds now the  even bigger deal for me  is that the regular lte speed is now  twice as fast  going from one gigabit per second to two  gigabits per second  matching up to speeds on samsung  flagship phones  just like last year we get wi-fi 6  bluetooth 5.0 and  the ultra wide u1 chip which the iphone  11  already had as far as the battery life  it should stay  basically the same according to apple's  tech specs  now one of the coolest new features is  the brand new  magsafe system basically the wireless  charging coil inside of every iphone 12  has new magnets built into it so you can  connect  any of apple's new magnetic magsafe  accessories  like the new wallet right onto the back  of the iphone itself  just using magnets there's also the new  cases  which have magnets built in so it simply  snaps on  without holding onto the sides of the  phone making it easier to put on and  take off  and you can place the magnetic wallet on  top of the magnetic  case as well which is really cool but  the best part is the new  magsafe wireless charger which is a very  compact  and slim charger that snaps onto the  back of the phone  and holds on magnetically so you can  still use your phone  while it's wirelessly charging and it  charges at up to 15 watts  compared to seven and a half watts for  regular qi chargers  they also showed off some new magsafe  chargers that are coming soon  like the max save duo the car mount and  the multi-charger dock now the biggest  difference is  in terms of the cameras so let's get  right into it the ultrawide lens is  basically identical between the 12 pro  and the 11 pro models but the wide  camera is getting huge  upgrades including a faster f 1.6  aperture  and a new seven element lens compared to  f 1.8 aperture with a six element lens  on the 11 pro model  and that's gonna improve improve  low-light camera performance  by up to 27 apple also mentioned that  the optical image stabilization  on the wide cameras is getting five  times  faster compared to the iphone 11 lineup  now as far as the telephoto lens is  basically the same on the regular iphone  12 pro model  you get 2x optical zoom and not  4x like a ton of channels misinterpreted  in recent leaks so it's a 4x optical  range  from the ultrawide to the telephoto and  thanks to the new sensors and super fast  a14 chip  we finally get night mode on all of the  cameras  as well as smart hdr3 with scene  detection  and deep fusion on every camera  including  the selfie as well we also get a brand  new image signal processor  for improved noise reduction and better  photos  now here's where it gets very  interesting the iphone 12 pro max  actually gets some exclusive camera  upgrades that the regular pro  doesn't get so let's get right into  those the pro max gets a brand new  wide camera sensor that is 47  larger and the pixels within that sensor  are now a larger 1.7 micrometers  this basically gives the pro max an even  better 87  improved low light performance over the  iphone 11 pro  and on top of that the 12 pro max gets  an exclusive  sensor shift optical image stabilization  feature  so you should get super smooth video and  super sharp photos  and we'll be testing that out very soon  so click that subscribe button below so  you don't miss out  on top of that the 12 pro max gets a  slightly longer  2.5 times optical zoom telephoto lens  with up to 12x digital zoom but the  aperture does get a little bit slower to  f 2.2  to allow for the extra zoom both of the  iphone 12 pro models come with the brand  new lidar scanner  which projects lasers and then detects  how long it takes to get back to the  camera  and then that allows you to use it with  augmented reality apps  like getting a 3d map of your room and  it actually helps the cameras as well  for example the lidar scanner will now  be used  to auto focus in the dark or for  nighttime shots  speeding up the time it takes to take  photos and  improving auto focus performance in the  dark by up to six  times not only that but it improves  depth tracking  for portrait mode photos and it even  finally enables portrait mode  for nighttime photos which the iphone 11  pro  didn't have now moving on to video  recording everything basically stays the  same  except for two brand new formats you can  now record at the same 4k 60 frames per  second as before  but you can now do it in dolby vision  hdr  which is a first time for any camera  ever because it requires the device to  grade the footage  and apple's algorithms are doing it  automatically  in real time as you're recording and  then later this year  apple is coming out with the new apple  pro raw feature  which will record in raw footage format  and automatically apply adjustments  using  machine learning and you can even go  into the photos app and edit the raw  footage  allowing for much more editing  capabilities compared to regular footage  and as a little bonus apple added a  night mode  time lapse feature which can be cool for  capturing stars  with higher quality now finally getting  into the prices  they're basically the same as before 999  dollars for the iphone 12 pro and 10.99  for the 12 pro max  but what's great this year is that they  now come with  double the storage 128 gigs compared to  64 gigs  that came with the iphone 11 pro models  the only downside is that you no longer  get earpods or a charger in the box  so if you don't already have one you're  gonna have to order those separately  so now that i covered all of the new  features let me get into the ones that  actually matter  in terms of upgradeability because in my  personal experience  the iphone 11 pro has been an excellent  phone if you love the flat edge design  then this is the best time to upgrade  because i'm willing to bet that apple is  sticking to this design  for the next few years so if you buy an  iphone 12  it's gonna look modern for years to come  of course you've also got the new a14  bionic chip  which improves performance and enables  all of those cool  new camera features so if you want to  see us test the real world performance  and benchmarks  subscribe right now so you don't miss  out now while apple hasn't revealed the  exact amount of ram  most leaks are pointing to the 12 pro  models getting 6 gigs  compared to 4 gigs on the iphone 11 pro  so this could be a huge deal  for using apps without them closing on  you now you might be saying  i don't need 5g but keep in mind that  the new modems  actually also improve regular 4g speed  as well  and it improves reliability compared to  the iphone 11 pro  so that by itself is great now if you're  someone who's all about the cameras  and that's the biggest priority for you  then i would definitely upgrade because  the 12 pro comes with new camera sensors  which have faster readouts allowing  apple to add those extra features like  the third generation  of smart hdr and everything else and  don't forget that the 12 pro max gets  even more camera features on top of that  and will definitely be testing them  it just sucks that you have to wait  another month before we can finally  start ordering the pro max models  now one feature that was missing is 120  hertz pro motion technology  and that's definitely disappointing  especially if you really wanted that  feature  and if you really do then i'd suggest  holding off because i'm fairly certain  that we're going to get it next year but  in general the iphone 11 pro is already  an  excellent phone and if you're happy with  everything about it  and you feel that the performance the  cellular service the battery life  the cameras and everything else about  the 11 pro  is already good enough for you then  don't upgrade unless you've got  too much cash to care but if you're  really interested in faster lte speeds  5g the new design the new mac save  feature  and camera performance improvements then  i definitely say that it's worth  upgrading even from the 11 pro  especially if your smartphone  is a big priority in your life but  because we don't yet have the iphone 12  pro in our hands  we don't know how good it'll truly be so  if you want to see a full comparison  between the 11 pro  and the 12 pro go ahead and tap the like  button and click the circle above so you  don't miss out  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video
 

